{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 33, :comments ["<b>Swear to me this day.</b> When Esau said, \"Why do I need the birthright?\" — meaning he did not want it — Jacob said to him, \"Swear to me that you do not want it and that you shall never inherit it,\" and he swore to him; and afterward he sold it to him and gave him the price, that is, the stew, that he had requested. And it is possible that Esau said, \"Why do I need the birthright? Behold, it is sold to you,\" and he (Jacob) said, \"Swear to me that you will never contest the sale,\" and Scripture says that he swore to him and sold it — as though it said he sold it and swore to him."], :book :genesis, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:34:55.231216434Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}